{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'yang\\\\.frontend/preferred|defn (standard|install-php|select)|1,325|legacy.*parity|parity.*quick' src test bin collab/yang-clojure -g '\"'!*.stdout.log'\"' -g '\"'!*.json'\"' -g '\"'!*.edn'\"' --max-count 8\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljs/datomworld/demo.cljs:100:(defn select-demo!\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795322379478-engineer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy-default-flip.prompt.md:57:Implementation on `feat/p3prime-descriptor-cljpy`, UNCOMMITTED (no commit authority). Final report: files added/changed per scope item; each gate with exact command + counts; py-v1 legacy corpus parity evidence; fresh goldens list; the cross-syntax unwind fixture description; ambiguities resolved with §/quotes; any gate not run and why.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795331164900-reviewer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy.prompt.md:23:My own runs: prelude-parity 35/221/0; the full legacy-corpus lane (oracle-parity+int-ops+int-conv+int-contract+int-literal+lower-portable+float-text+prelude-parity) 85/1428/0 (engineer-captured log, invocation verified); clojure-test+callsite+effect 160/1677/0; wedge 1/7/0; LaTTe 37/2608/0; descriptor-profile+catalog+query 43/540/0; deps analyzer clean; js/php diffs empty. 4-host legs captured by the engineer: Node legacy oracles 9/27, Jolt legacy, Dart gates (verify the code claims, not the suites).\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795331164900-reviewer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:43:   - `yin.repl.frontends/standard` (`frontends.cljc:394-399`) installs both `\"py-v1\"` and `\"clojure-core-v1\"` revisions of `:yang/python` and sets `:yang.frontend/preferred [:yang/python \"clojure-core-v1\"]` on the immutable catalog.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795331164900-reviewer-p3prime-descriptor-cljpy.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:44:   - `yang.frontend/select` (`frontend.cljc:216-227`) resolves ID-only requests via `:yang.frontend/preferred` when present and matching, while preserving explicit `[id revision]` pins and ambiguity refusals for unconfigured multi-revision frontends.\nsrc/dev/affected.clj:316:(defn select\nsrc/dev/affected.clj:396:(defn select-subsystems\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795455124699-reviewer-p4-php-clojure-core.prompt.md:23:descriptor 6/320/0; lower-portable+prelude 41/1627/0; deps clean. Engineer-captured: profile suites 55/2537/0 (JVM), Node/Dart/Jolt lanes, legacy parity 1,325 fixtures zero differences (518 permutations + 271 PHPT), the 3 python pin errors (pre-existing red #6, reproduced at clean base). OPEN items the implementer declared: the wide JVM e2e run had no final counts; the optional full-permutation oracle file is absent from the checkout — weigh whether either blocks approval.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795455124699-reviewer-p4-php-clojure-core.prompt.md:28:2. **Legacy `php-v1` preservation:** descriptor pins today's `'php/*` hooks 1:1; the 1,325-fixture parity is the evidence — scrutinize the `yang.php.antlr.lower` hunks for anything beyond descriptor reads.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795455124699-reviewer-p4-php-clojure-core.glm.findings.md:11:Legacy `php-v1` preservation reads clean: every legacy hunk is an `app* 'php/x` to `(hook ctx :php/x ...)` swap where `legacy-hooks` maps the role to the identical symbol; literal strategies reproduce the old nodes exactly (verified: `(u/sexp->uast :php/null)` is node-identical to `(u/lit :php/null)` for the request default; the forced `bits 64` in `builtin-constant-node` keeps positive builtin ints on `php/int-lit`; the `2**53` int boundary via bit-length 53 equals the old `max-safe-int` compare). The clj.php adapter has zero provenance doors (only `clj/make-callable`, `clj/invoke-callable`, `clj/prim-get`), mirrors the landed `clj.py` `_run`/policy pattern, and the stream-output gate matches native `php/run-main` (body record `stream/put!` only when output is non-empty and a response stream is attached; the fixture proves both cases in bundled+linked). The DEFAULT flip reuses the P3' mechanism with a backward-compatible generalization (`:yang.frontend/preferred` as map or pair), in-flight snapshots retained, bare compiler calls keep the native pin (`:or {descriptor legacy-descriptor}`). Capability honesty: all 27 declared capabilities trace to enforcement sites; `admit-key?` flows through `clj/collection-key`'s `:coll/unsupported-key` policy; reserved-door ban holds and is fixture-probed. Fences hold: no `yang/typescript/` changes, php prelude modules untouched, `:cljd/:jolt` portability gates, canonical ordering, boxed float paths throughout `clj.php`, and the cljs `1e15` postwalk is correctly `:cljs`-scoped.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795455124699-reviewer-p4-php-clojure-core.glm.findings.md:23:**NOTE | OPEN items** | Neither blocks approval. (1) The wide JVM e2e run lacking final counts is an evidence gap on the slow tier, not a defect: the legacy emission is symbol- and node-identical by construction (verified by reading; corroborated by lower-portable+prelude 41/1627/0 and the captured 1,325-fixture zero-diff parity incl. 518 permutations + 271 PHPT). (2) The absent full-permutation oracle file is the shiva-recorded exhaustive corpus (`test/yang/php/antlr/permutations.cljc` header); the 518-permutation tier that *was* run plus the PHPT suite already cover the refcount/reference machinery the refactor could have disturbed. Recommendation: complete the wide e2e run before merging this branch to master.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795455124699-reviewer-p4-php-clojure-core.glm.findings.md:44:**F2 (MEDIUM, bare isset native refusal) - CLOSED.** `isset-loc` (`lower.cljc:1089-1093`) routes the empty-path case to `isset-var` only under `legacy?`; the persistent profile uses the same null-compare as the offset path and `empty()`. The composite answer is PHP-faithful for bare variables (PHP isset = set-and-not-null; an unbound read is null here): `isset($missing)`/`isset($n=null)` -> false, `isset($f=false, $z=0, $s='')` -> true, multi-argument isset reduces conjunctively, and the in-function form works over the lexical cells. Fixture `:150-151` covers top-level and in-function, missing/null and falsy-but-assigned. Legacy emission is untouched (the guard is `(and (legacy? ctx) ...)`), consistent with the zero-mismatch parity rerun.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1795455124699-reviewer-p4-php-clojure-core.glm.findings.md:50:Orchestrator-verified gates accepted: descriptor 7/370/0 (was 6/320/0 - the new deftest + fixtures), portable+prelude+request 44/1662/0, legacy parity 1,325 fixtures zero mismatches, deps clean, scoped e2e 4/86/0. The wide e2e run remains open as already noted in r1 (non-blocking; complete before merge).\ntest/dao/host/gate_test.clj:96:(defn select-arms\nsrc/dev/yang/php/phpt.clj:25:(defn select\ntest/yang/python/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:361:        legacy-catalog (assoc catalog :yang.frontend/preferred [:yang/python \"py-v1\"])\ntest/yang/php/antlr/phpt.clj:33:(defn selected-path?\ntest/yang/php/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc:210:        switched (assoc-in catalog [:yang.frontend/preferred :yang/php] \"php-v1\")\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:154:(defn standard\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:164:                                true (assoc-in [:yang.frontend/preferred :yang/php] \"clojure-core-v1\")]))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc:169:          (assoc-in [:yang.frontend/preferred :yang/python] \"clojure-core-v1\"))\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:193:(defn select\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:203:   :yang.frontend/preferred as an id-to-revision map or an [id revision] pair.\"\nsrc/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc:216:        preference (:yang.frontend/preferred catalog)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
